{{also|in-kind}}
==English==

===Etymology===
A [[calque]] translation of the {{etyl|la}} phrase {{term|in specie||lang=la}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|pos=[[in]] [[kind]]}}

# (paying or giving) with goods or services (as opposed to cash)
#: ''I made some donations to the charity, not in money, but in kind, such as non-perishable food.''
# {{idiom}} In a [[reciprocal]] manner; in a similar way; in the same kind.
#: ''I kissed him, and he responded '''in kind''' and kissed me back.''

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|with goods or service}} [[in trade]]
* {{sense|in a similar way}} [[equivalently]], [[reciprocally]], [[similarly]]

